// Title: Potential Signing Bypass Via Windows Developer Features
// Sigma ID: a383dec4-deec-4e6e-913b-ed9249670848
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects when a user enable developer features such as "Developer Mode" or "Application
//   Sideloading". Which allows the user to install untrusted packages.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/inside-malicious-windows-apps-for-malware-deployment/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_systemsettingsadminflows_turn_on_dev_features.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SystemSettingsAdminFlows.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SystemSettingsAdminFlows.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains "TurnOnDeveloperFeatures" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "DeveloperUnlock" or ProcessCommandLine contains "EnableSideloading")
